## Test Criteria (ground truth — written from actual source; overrides any conflicting AC)
- LivePreviewProvider is defined in src/pages/_app.tsx and wraps the entire app inside MyApp via <LivePreviewProvider>.
- LivePreviewProvider initializes ContentstackLivePreview.init with { stackSdk: Stack as any, enable: true, ssr: false } inside a useEffect.
- ContentstackLivePreview.onEntryChange registers a callback that reads document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-cslp]') and extracts attributes 'data-cslp-content-type-uid' and 'data-cslp-entry-uid'.
- If contentTypeUid or entryUid is absent from the [data-cslp] element, the onEntryChange callback returns early and does not call setPreviewPage.
- The onEntryChange callback creates a query via Stack.ContentType(contentTypeUid).Entry(entryUid).toJSON() and calls .fetch().
- On successful fetch, the callback calls setPreviewPage([result]) where result is typed as IContentstackPage.
- On fetch error, the callback calls .catch(() => {}) — errors are swallowed silently and prior previewPage state is preserved.
- LivePreviewProvider state is: const [previewPage, setPreviewPage] = useState<[IContentstackPage] | undefined>(undefined).
- LivePreviewContext is exported from src/context/contentstackContext.tsx with shape { previewPage?: [IContentstackPage]; setPreviewPage: Dispatch<SetStateAction<[IContentstackPage] | undefined>> } and default value { previewPage: undefined, setPreviewPage: () => undefined }.
- useContent hook in src/hooks/useContent.ts reads both ContentstackContext and LivePreviewContext via useContext.
- useContent computes effectiveContent = previewPage ? { ...content, page: previewPage } : content — when previewPage is defined, it overrides the page property of the existing content.
- useContent returns { getContentByKey } where getContentByKey calls getValue<T>(effectiveContent, path, defaultValue).
- When previewPage is undefined (no preview signal), effectiveContent equals the original content from ContentstackContext, so published content is rendered unchanged.
- Homepage component in src/components/pages/Homepage.tsx receives props of type IHomepageProps { page: [IContentstackPage] } and does NOT directly call useContent — it reads page from props.
- Homepage extracts pageComponents via getValue<PageComponents>(page, '0.modular_blocks', []) and recentNews via getValue<IRecentNews>(page, '0.recent_news', {}).
- IMPLEMENTATION CONFLICT: VC requires that when a draft entry change is signaled for the MX Homepage, the rendered Homepage shows draft content; Homepage.tsx receives page from props and does not call useContent, so the LivePreviewContext override may not reach the Homepage component itself — only child components that call useContent would receive preview data.
- IMPLEMENTATION CONFLICT: VC requires that when a draft entry change is signaled while the page is in a protected or gated state, the page does not render draft content; the onEntryChange callback in _app.tsx contains NO check for protected/gated state — it unconditionally calls setPreviewPage with the fetched draft entry.
- Stack is exported from src/services/contentstack.ts as contentstack.Stack(options) with live_preview config { enable: true, management_token: PREVIEW_TOKEN, host: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST || 'api.contentstack.io' }.
- getSingleEntry in src/services/contentstack.ts returns Promise<IContentstackPage> and accepts params { contentTypeUid, entryUid, lang, referenceFieldPath, jsonRtePath, only, except, cachePolicy }.
- IContentstackPage interface in src/interface/content/page.ts has fields: uid: string, title: string, url: string, page_components?: PageComponents, include_on_page_navigation: boolean, publish_date: string, _content_type_uid?: string.
- INewsArticlePage extends IContentstackPage and adds news_article_components: PageComponents.
- getContentStackNewsArticles in src/api/utils/_contentstack_getNewsArticles.ts uses Stack.ContentType(ContentTypes.NewsArticle).Query() and returns { entries: result[0], count: result[1] }.
- The onEntryChange callback supports multiple successive calls — each call fetches the entry and calls setPreviewPage with the new result, so successive draft changes update previewPage state in sequence.
- There is no debounce, throttle, or deduplication logic in the onEntryChange callback — every entry change event triggers a new fetch and setPreviewPage call.
- ContentstackLivePreview is imported from '@contentstack/live-preview-utils' in src/pages/_app.tsx.
- Stack is imported from 'services/contentstack' in src/pages/_app.tsx.
- LivePreviewContext is imported from 'context/contentstackContext' in src/pages/_app.tsx.
- IContentstackPage is imported from 'interface/content/page' in src/pages/_app.tsx.

